{
  "name": "Approval · 2 Decide",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Approval · Decide\nWhat an approver reaches from the link. Two public webhooks, guarded by the token in the link.\n\n**Open** (`GET approval/open`) only shows a page. A request that is still open gets two buttons. One that expired or was decided gets \"expired at ...\" or \"already approved by ... at ...\", and the visit is logged. Opening decides nothing, so a mail scanner or a link preview cannot approve.\n\n**Decide** (`POST approval/decide`) is the button. The decision is **one conditional update**: `request_id` matches, `status` is `pending`, `expires_at` is later than now. Whoever gets that update decided the request; every other click, late or repeated, reads the row and is told what happened. It works without the sweep having run.\n\nOnly the click that won an **approve** reaches **Do the approved thing**. Replace that node with your action; `request_id` goes along as `Idempotency-Key`. **Tell the requester** reports approved and rejected.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "0ecbe6dd-af31-479c-80e1-0d3482c87841",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -620
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
